Given, $V_{1}=120 \mathrm{ V}, V_{2}=200 \mathrm{ V}
Since, potential on each capacitor is zero when they are connected$ in parallel. Hence, charge on each capacitor must be equal with unlike polarities together.\begin{aligned}$\text{ i.e. }$& q_{1} &=q_{2} \\
\Rightarrow & C_{1} V_{1} &=C_{2} V_{2} \\
\Rightarrow & C_{1} $\times120 \text{$ and $} =C_{2} \times200 \\
\Rightarrow \text{ and } \text{ and } 3 C_{1} \text{ and } =5 C_{2}
\end{aligned}$

The given combination is a balanced condition of Wheatstone bridge because potential at $C$ and $D$ points is same.
